    {
      "musicID": "botw_tower_lake",
      "musicName": "Sheikah Tower (Lake Tower Version)",
      "linkedAlbumID": "wally71551_og",
      "seriesID": "loz",
      "projectID": "botw",
      "releaseDate": "2017-10-01",
      "linkedAlbumTrack": 18,
      "description": "I originally set out to create one theme, but decided I could variate more and create a much more interesting piece by creating a separate piece for each of other Sheikah Towers in the game. This one is based on the Lake Tower, which overlooks Lake Hylia.\n\nTo start, the arrangement is very light and simple, contrasting synthesized waves with a grand piano and choir. The piece builds into a repeat, where tremolo strings and flute join the piece, as well as some light percussion.\n\nThe piece builds further by adding more percussion and using the lower end of the piano to add some textural depth to the piece. The instrumentation of a string section was used to signify the grandeur and scale of Lake Hylia, helping the piece further fit in this setting along with the ambience in the background.\n\nThe penultimate section uses 2 phrases from the music for the Story Trailer shown off at the Nintendo Switch Presentation in January 2017, but at a much slower tempo. The melody is variated to give a melancholic feel to showcase the deep and dark history that Hyrule has suffered through in this game.\n\nThe slow melody and moving chords of this section are contrasted by the quick main motif of the Sheikah Tower theme scattered throughout this section of the piece. Synths are still used to show the contrast of the advanced Sheikah technology against the ruined Hyrule.",
      "youtubeLink": "https://youtu.be/cOexOVmwzUI",
      "musicType": "Remix"
